.TH USBRADIOPLUS-TUNE 8 "August 2026" "USBRadioPlus alpha" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
usbradioplus-tune \- tune and monitor a USBRadioPlus radio interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usbradioplus-tune
.br
.B usbradioplus-rxlevel
[menu|calibrate [seconds]|status|cancel|save]
.br
.B usbradioplus-processing-tune
[--check] [--offline] [--config path] [--lock path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These utilities configure USBRadioPlus from a keyboard-operated terminal.
Run them as root on the Asterisk node. Changes made by the interactive menus
take effect immediately; use the explicit save command to retain radio tuning
values after a restart.
.PP
Menu buttons use consistent action names. Select opens the highlighted item,
Apply commits an edit, Back returns one menu level, Exit leaves the utility,
Cancel abandons an edit, and Close dismisses information without changing it.
.SH USBRADIOPLUS-TUNE
The main menu operates on the active RadioPlus device. It provides:
.TP
.B Select active USB device
Choose one configured radio interface. Swap exchanges USB assignments between
two configured interfaces; it does not exchange their radio settings.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX noise level
With no carrier present, adjust USB capture level and the DSP carrier-squelch
starting point. This requires flat discriminator audio and should be followed
by receiver-level and squelch verification.
.TP
.B Set RX voice level using display
Show a live deviation bar, then accept a 0--999 receive voice setting. Press
any key to leave the live display and reach the setting prompt.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX CTCSS level
Measure received CTCSS and adjust decoder level. Apply a carrier with the
configured tone and specified tone deviation before selecting this action.
.TP
.B Set RX squelch level
Display current DSP signal strength and accept a 0--999 squelch setting. Higher
numbers require a stronger signal to open.
.TP
.B Set TX voice level
Set the 0--999 mixer level for the output carrying voice or composite audio.
When test-tone keying is enabled, the action keys PTT and sends 1 kHz for five
seconds.
.TP
.B Set auxiliary voice level
Set the 0--999 level on the output configured as auxvoice. The action is
unavailable unless one output mixer carries auxvoice.
.TP
.B Set TX CTCSS level
Set CTCSS deviation from 0--999. When test-tone keying is enabled, the action
keys PTT and sends CTCSS for five seconds.
.TP
.B Auto-detect RX voice level
Adjust recovered voice gain from a received 1 kHz tone at 3 kHz deviation.
This action requires flat discriminator audio and a steady calibrated signal.
.TP
.B Echo mode
Return received audio to the transmitter for alignment. Disable it when the
test is complete.
.TP
.B Flash transmitter
Send three one-second PTT and 1 kHz tone bursts separated by 1.5 seconds.
.TP
.B Carrier and CTCSS source
Select the COS and tone indication sources supported by usbradioplus.conf(5).
.TP
.B Options
Set RX boost, TX boost, RX demodulation, RX-on and TX-off delays, transmit
pre-limiting, limiting-only operation, and USB output A and B routing.
It also sets the transmit soft-limiter onset from 5000 through 13000, the
duplex-3 repeat level from 0 through 999, and whether duplex-3 repeat audio uses
the CM119 hardware mixer or the native software path.
.TP
.B Configure audio processing
Open
.BR usbradioplus-processing-tune .
On return, the radio tuning menu refreshes its displayed values.
.TP
.B Print current parameter values
Report the selected interface, USB device, output routing, and principal RX/TX
levels.
.TP
.B Live statistics and status
Display RX or TX peak, RMS, clipping, COS, CTCSS, and PTT state. Press Enter
to return. TX statistics report that PTT is clear when the transmitter is idle.
.TP
.B Save current parameter values
Write device selection, signal sources, mixer and radio levels, squelch,
delays, boosts, transmitter processing selections, and limiter setpoint to
usbradioplus.conf. EEPROM values are also written when EEPROM storage is enabled.
.SH USBRADIOPLUS-RXLEVEL
.TP
.B menu
Open the numbered receive calibration menu. This is the default action.
.TP
.B calibrate [seconds]
Collect closed-squelch noise and at least one second of COR-qualified receive
audio for 2--600 seconds. The default is 30 seconds. On completion, report the
recommended pre- and post-squelch gains, peaks, and ADC rail counts, then save
the gains.
.TP
.B status
Report whether calibration is running, current gain recommendations, noise and
signal peaks, sample counts, and ADC rail counts.
.TP
.B cancel
Stop a running calibration without changing gains.
.TP
.B save
Write the current pre- and post-squelch gain values to usbradioplus.conf.
.SH USBRADIOPLUS-PROCESSING-TUNE
The processing menu selects local receiver, linked audio, or voice and telemetry.
Only controls applicable to the selected source are shown. Stage toggles use
single keys and the arrow, Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Escape, B, and Q keys. Numeric
pages validate both the documented range and dependent relationships such as a
low-pass cutoff being above its high-pass cutoff.
.PP
The Filters page groups every fixed filter that applies to the selected source.
For local receive it selects or disables CTCSS notch, comb, or high-pass
filtering and sets the applicable cutoff or notch width. For voice and telemetry
it enables or disables the transmit brick-wall band-pass and post-limiter
low-pass and sets their cutoff frequencies. Dynamics pages contain the
high-pass and low-pass detector filters for AGC, expansion, and compression.
.PP
Each accepted edit is written atomically and reloaded. If validation or reload
fails, the preceding file and active settings are restored. The main menu can
create a timestamped backup or restore the configuration from the start of the
session.
.TP
.B --check
Validate prerequisites and confirm that the configured local, link, and
voice/telemetry sections can be read.
.TP
.B --offline
With --check, do not require Asterisk or the terminal menu package. This is
intended for installation and package tests.
.TP
.B --config path
Use another processing configuration for --check.
.TP
.B --lock path
Use another menu lock file.
.SH SERVICE-MONITOR PROCEDURE
Use a dummy load or authorized test frequency. Set capture gain first with an
unmodulated receiver and verify that ADC rail counts remain zero. Apply a
calibrated 1 kHz signal at system deviation and set recovered RX voice level.
Apply the configured CTCSS tone at the specified tone deviation and verify
decode margin.
.PP
Key into a service monitor, set voice peak deviation, then set CTCSS deviation.
Verify peak and RMS level, clipping, occupied bandwidth, PTT operation, and
tone turn-off behavior before saving. Repeat checks after reconnecting USB and
after restarting Asterisk.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf
Radio-interface and saved tuning values.
.TP
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus-processing.conf
Optional processing graphs.
.TP
.B /run/lock/usbradioplus-processing-tune.lock
Processing-menu single-instance lock.
